{
  "about": "Graphs whose style graph moves its links (editor spec §7: links_show_flow, flow_in_style_graph, motion_not_alone), drawn the same by the plugin's core and by graph_svg.py. Each case is a note's gql blocks, each block a list of lines, and the view it is drawn in, if any (its name only: the whole graph is drawn, styled as that view is). For every case both give the same problems reading each style, the same links moving and how, and, for every graph drawn, the same Graphviz source in each direction laid out, byte for byte: each moving link's label opened by its icon, its classes, and dashes drawn dashed. The expected answers are the core's, run live: packages/core/test/link-flow-parity.test.js holds graph_svg.py to the core on these cases, and tests/test_graph_svg_flow.py does the same from the Python side.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "dashes on every link, the link drawn backwards moving backwards along its line",
